<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Douglas, Isle of Man</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Douglas is the capital and largest town of the Isle of Man, on the island's east coast. It grew from a fishing port into a busy trading town and, in the 19th century, a popular seaside resort, and replaced Castletown as the seat of government in 1869. It is home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tynwald">Tynwald</a> and the island's financial services industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/douglas-isle-of-man.jpg" alt="Douglas, Isle of Man" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zairon · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Douglas_Douglas_Head_View_to_Douglas_Harbour_03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
